In JSTL, you can use the `<c:forEach>` tag to loop over a collection. However, if you want to loop a specified number of times, you can create a simple collection with that number of elements and then loop over it. Here's an example:

```xml
<%@ taglib prefix="c" uri="http://java.sun.com/jsp/jstl/core" %>

<%
    // Define the number of iterations
    int iterations = 5;

    // Create a List with the specified number of elements
    List<Integer> numbers = new ArrayList<Integer>();
