To dynamically set the background gradient colors, you can use the `GradientDrawable` class. This class allows you to create and manipulate gradient drawings programmatically. Here's how you can achieve this:

First, remove the gradient definition from your XML layout file for the custom title bar. Instead, create a `GradientDrawable` instance in your Java code and apply it to your `LinearLayout` programmatically.

Here's an example:

```java
// Create a GradientDrawable instance
GradientDrawable gradientDrawable = new GradientDrawable(
    GradientDrawable.Orientation.TOP_BOTTOM, new int[] { getResources().getColor(R.color.start_color), getResources().getColor(R.color.end_color) }
);

// Set the gradient drawable as the background of your LinearLayout
LinearLayout customTitleBar = (LinearLayout) findViewById(R.id.custom_title_bar);
customTitleBar.setBackground(gradientDrawable);
```

Replace `R.color.start_color` and `R.color.end_color` with your desired color resources. You can dynamically set these colors based on your requirements, such as user preferences or other runtime conditions.

This approach allows you to set the background gradient colors dynamically without hardcoding them in your XML layout file. You can easily adjust the colors based on various conditions or user inputs.

