This makes more sense when you think about how the parallelization goes. Many machines will each reduce their data to a single object, and those objects will then be reduced to a final output. Of course, this may happen in more than one layer if there is a lot of data. Here's a simple example of how you might use the map/reduce framework to count words in a list:

list = ['a', 'foo', 'bar', 'foobar', 'foo', 'a', 'bar', 'bar', 'bar', 'bar', 'foo']
